# llm-guard.baseline — exceptions for scripts/llm-guard.py, each VERIFIED BY HAND.
#
# Format:  <doc>  TAB  <key>  TAB  <why this finding is not a defect>
#   key = <cited-path>:<lo>-<hi>   for a `citations` finding
#         symbol:<name>            for a `symbols` finding whose name belongs to another repo
#
# Only `citations` and cross-repo `symbols` findings can be listed here. `paths`, `forbidden`,
# `phantom`, `version`, out-of-bounds and `vacuous` are deterministic and always fail.
#
# An entry matching nothing is reported as `baseline-stale` and FAILS, so this file cannot rot
# into a blanket exemption.  Re-derive with: python3 scripts/llm-guard.py --no-baseline
#
# The public qb-io pump named by the module guide lives in qb, not qbm-pgsql. The root guard
# resolves it against the qb source; this standalone module guard records that boundary.
llm/qbm-pgsql.llm.md	symbol:run_once	qb::io::async::run_once is defined in qb/src/qb/io/async/listener.h:1618; qbm-pgsql only calls it.
